1️⃣ Arithmetic Operators  (binary if 2 operands unary if 1 operand i++ jaise ) if ++a tgen pehele increase hoga and then use hoga if a++ then pehel use hoga badhega 

Used for calculations.

+   // addition
-   // subtraction
*   // multiplication
/   // division
%   // modulus (remainder)

Increment Confusion (Very Important)
int a = 5;

System.out.println(a++);  // prints 5
System.out.println(a);    // 6

Post-increment → use first, then increase.

int b = 5;

System.out.println(++b);  // prints 6

Pre-increment → increase first, then use.



3️⃣ Relational (Comparison) Operators

Used in conditions.

==  // equal to
!=  // not equal
>   // greater
<   // smaller
>=  // greater equal
<=  // smaller equal
this will return me true or false

4️⃣ Logical Operators

Used mostly in if conditions.

&&  // AND
||  // OR
!   // NOT

Example:

int age = 20;

if(age > 18 && age < 25) {
    System.out.println("Young Adult");
}
⚠ Short Circuit Concept (Very Important)
if(false && true)  // second part not even checked

&& and || use short-circuit evaluation.
this also gives me output as true or false


5️⃣ Assignment Operators
=   // assign
+=
-=
*=
/=
%=

Example:

int a = 5;
a += 3;   // same as a = a +3
basically = se pehele likhna he